# FAKE_USER_DEC — what stays out of source control.
#
# The rule: track everything a new developer needs to reproduce the project,
# and nothing a command can regenerate. Source, tests, docs, screenshots,
# .env.example and the small input datasets are all tracked.

# --- python ---------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.example IS tracked; it documents every key with no value in it.
.env
.env.local

# --- legacy model pickles (69-105 MB each, GitHub rejects >100 MB) ---------
# These belong to website/ and FAKE_PROFILE_TRAIN_CODE/, both superseded. Their
# source is tracked; the weights are not, and nothing current loads them.
# `*.pkl.backup` needs its own line: `*.pkl` does not match it, and one 69 MB
# file slipped into the first staging run because of exactly that.
*.pkl
*.pkl.*
*.joblib.backup

# --- trained artifacts -----------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated by `python -m ml.train_xgb` (see README "Train the model").
# The metadata beside each one IS tracked: it is the record of the run whose
# numbers the README and docs/PAPER_ALIGNMENT.md quote.
*.joblib

# --- generated datasets ----------------------------------------------------
# Both are written by `python -m ml.generate_dataset`, which is seeded, so a
# clone reproduces them byte-for-byte. data/dataset.csv and
# advanced_instagram_fake_real_data_filled_bio.csv are NOT ignored - they are
# supplied inputs, only ~1 MB each, and the control experiment needs them.
data/paper_signal.csv
data/synthetic_signal.csv

# --- byte-identical duplicates of website/dataset_original.csv --------------
# Three copies of one file (md5 3519671bd2b3). One is kept, at
# website/dataset_original.csv... which is itself one of the three, so keep the
# copy the docs actually cite and drop the rest.
papper/dataset.csv
FAKE_PROFILE_TRAIN_CODE/dataset.csv

# --- archives and scratch ---------------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.log
.DS_Store

# --- android/gradle build output (none tracked here, kept for safety) -------
build/
.gradle/
node_modules/

# --- one-off scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
# A 5-byte file containing a single emoji. Not source, not data, not a test.
test.txt
